    "text": "There is a pair of fixed, parallel rails of negligible resistance in a horizontal plane, at a distance of <math><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The rails are connected, at one of their ends to an ideal battery of EMF&nbsp;<math><mn>0.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>, as shown in the figure. The system is placed in a vertically downward and perpendicular magnetic field of magnetic induction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. A metal rod of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> is placed perpendicularly on the rails. The rod and rails are frictionless. The magnitude of force, which is to be exerted on the rod in order to move it with a constant speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>–</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> in the direction shown, is<br />\r<br />\r<img height=\"89\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ieocapniquntshonpsvfaoegfuwknehwjacjiukzgodvfkqmbh.jpeg\" width=\"203\" />",
